-- Q3277: Advanced Lease Transactions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["A failed sale where the seller-lessee retains the asset and records a financing obligation","An operating lease with the seller-lessee as the lessee of the arrangement","A capital lease with full gain recognition on the date of the transaction","An off-balance-sheet arrangement with no impact on the seller-lessee''s statements"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 842-40, when a sale-leaseback fails the sale criteria because a repurchase option prevents transfer of control under ASC 606, the asset remains on the seller-lessee''s books and the proceeds are recorded as a financing obligation. No sale or leaseback is recognized.
Wrong (B): A failed sale-leaseback is not classified as an operating lease. Because the sale did not occur, the transaction is treated as a financing arrangement, not a lease.
Wrong (C): No gain can be recognized because the transaction does not qualify as a sale. The asset is never derecognized, so there is no basis for gain recognition.
Wrong (D): The transaction is on-balance-sheet. The seller-lessee retains the asset and records the proceeds as a financial liability.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3277;

-- Q3282: Advanced Lease Transactions [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Recognized as revenue by the lessee over the lease term","Expensed by the lessee as incurred in the period received","Recorded as an increase to the lessee''s lease liability balance","Applied as a reduction to the measurement of the ROU asset"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 842-20-30-5, lease incentives received by the lessee, such as tenant improvement allowances, reduce the measurement of the right-of-use asset. This reflects that the incentive lowers the lessee''s effective cost of the lease and results in lower amortization over the term.
Wrong (A): Lease incentives are not revenue. They are part of the lease consideration that reduces the ROU asset, not income to the lessee.
Wrong (B): The incentive is not expensed when received. It is integrated into the ROU asset measurement and affects amortization over the lease term.
Wrong (C): Lease incentives reduce the ROU asset, not increase the lease liability. The liability reflects the present value of lease payments, not incentives received.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3282;

-- Q3284: Advanced Lease Transactions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Included in the initial lease liability measurement along with fixed payments","Deferred until year-end and recognized as a single cumulative adjustment","Estimated at inception and capitalized as part of the right-of-use asset","Excluded from the lease liability and expensed when the triggering event occurs"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 842-10-15-37, variable lease payments that depend on sales or usage are excluded from the lease liability and ROU asset measurement. They are recognized as expense in the period the triggering event occurs, here when monthly sales exceed $100,000.
Wrong (A): Sales-based variable payments are excluded from the initial lease liability. Only fixed payments and variable payments tied to an index or rate are included in the measurement.
Wrong (B): Variable lease payments are not deferred. They are expensed in the specific period the contingency is resolved, not accumulated for year-end recognition.
Wrong (C): Sales-contingent payments cannot be reliably estimated at inception and are not capitalized. ASC 842 excludes them from the ROU asset measurement entirely.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3284;

-- Q3285: Advanced Lease Transactions [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Always the risk-free rate regardless of whether the implicit rate is known","The weighted average cost of capital for the lessee''s overall operations","The prime rate published by the lessee''s primary banking institution","The rate implicit in the lease if determinable; otherwise the incremental borrowing rate"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 842-20-30-3, the lessee uses the rate implicit in the lease if it can be readily determined. If not, the lessee uses its incremental borrowing rate. Private companies may elect the risk-free rate as a practical expedient, but it is not required.
Wrong (A): The risk-free rate is only available as an optional practical expedient for private companies. It is not the default rate, and public companies may not use it.
Wrong (B): WACC reflects overall capital structure and is not the rate prescribed by ASC 842 for discounting lease payments.
Wrong (C): The prime rate is a general market benchmark unrelated to the lease-specific discount rate required by ASC 842.$EXPL$
