-- Q3288: Advanced Lease Transactions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Derecognize the old lease entirely and record a completely new lease at current terms","Record the five-year extension as a separate lease independent of the original","Make no accounting change until the original ten-year lease term fully expires","Remeasure the lease liability at revised payments using a revised discount rate and adjust the ROU asset"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 842-10-25-1, a term extension is a lease modification. The lessee remeasures the lease liability using remaining payments, including the extension, discounted at a revised rate determined at the modification date. The ROU asset is adjusted by the same amount as the liability change.
Wrong (A): A term extension does not require derecognizing the existing lease. The modification adjusts the existing lease balances rather than replacing them entirely.
Wrong (B): A term extension that modifies the existing lease cannot be treated as a separate lease. It changes the scope and payments of the original arrangement.
Wrong (C): Delaying recognition until the original term expires would misstate the lease obligation. The modification must be reflected when it occurs.$EXPL$
